istance":0.3135,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.3289,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Anthony Campanile"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The 49ers are 7-1 through week 9 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 235 to 156. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 1st in EPA per play and the defense 8th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the highest pre-snap motion rate in the league.","offense":"The 49ers have one of the most efficient offenses in the league so far, ranking in the top eight in all five main efficiency measures. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the highest pre-snap motion rate and the 3rd highest under center rate in the league. Brock Purdy has run the passing game, with George Kittle leading the team in targets.","defense":"The 49ers have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 8th or better in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been explosive play rate allowed, where it ranks 1st, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 27th. Keion White has led the way with 3.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 5th lowest in the league.","special":"The 49ers have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 50% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 70% of field goals, which is one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 8% of the money on the books. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Brock Purdy has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,980 yards. George Kittle has been the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 483 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Christian McCaffrey and Kaelon Black. On defense, Keion White leads the team with 3.5 sacks and Renardo Green has picked off 4 passes.","coaching":"Kyle Shanahan is calling the offense as head coach and Raheem Morris is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 and 2023 Lions, both under Ben Johnson. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Panthers under Ejiro Evero and the 2025 Commanders.","trends":"The offense went from 6th in EPA per play in 2025 to 1st so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 24th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 8th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 10% to 3%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}